    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0765" n="1599" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/119</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-04T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 6, 12.43
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2575. For War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Your 1378, January 26 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 6 p.m. In Dresel’s
                    absence inform you that Foreign Office has replied to Legation’s memorandum
                    [which] requests elimination of words “of American origin,” as indicated your
                    telegram, and adding that Department of Public Economy is quite in accord to
                    suppress the words in question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
